course: dictionary
lesson: 7610
title: Prison and its two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Prison has two. The first is a real building where people who have broken the law are kept as a punishment. The second is a feeling: a place or situation where someone feels trapped, with no way out.
explain: «While Toad was in prison, the river-bankers stood up for him.» The words stood up for him tell you that Toad was locked away in a real place. Ask: what meaning would fit here? Try it in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the feeling meaning is clear from the other words. Ella says, «Homework every night feels like a prison.» Nobody is locked up, but she feels stuck and cannot get away. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: Prison means a building where people who have broken the law are kept as a punishment, or a place or situation where someone feels trapped.
fact: Phrases you may see are go to prison, in prison, prison officer and prison cell.
fact: «The Bastille» was a prison fortress in Paris, and people took it on 14 July 1789.
fact: In the UK and Ireland people also say jail or gaol. In the USA, jail is for short stays and prison is for long ones.
exercise: «While Toad was in prison, the river-bankers stood up for him.» In this sentence, what does prison mean? | A happy family meal at home | A ship sailing across the sea | *A building where people who have broken the law are kept
exercise: Ella says, «Homework every night feels like a prison.» What does prison mean here? | *A place or situation where someone feels trapped | A building for people who have broken the law | A large garden with a high wall
exercise: «In prison Joseph helped the other prisoners.» Find and copy one word that means people who are kept in prison. | *prisoners | Joseph | helped | other
test: What does prison mean in «a mam in prison»? | A bright shop window | *A building where people who have broken the law are kept | A feeling of being trapped at school
test: Which sentence uses prison for a feeling, not a building? | The prison cell had one small window. | *I felt like I was in prison all week, stuck indoors with no way out. | The prison officer locked the gate at six.
exam: In the USA, which word is used for a long stay in a place where people are kept? | Gaol | *Prison | Servo | Jail
